          "settings": {
            "question": "When do I switch from the balm to the cream?",
            "answer": "<p>Restore Balm carries roughly the first two weeks while the skin closes. Once flaking is finished and there are no open patches, step down to Recovery Cream daily. That's the jar you'll use for as long as you own the tattoo.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q-sealed": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Why is it sealed as a set?",
            "answer": "<p>Because the routine is the product. The first two weeks decide how the piece settles; the years after decide how it looks in a decade. Selling the balm on its own would sell you half a job, so it's one set, one price, never sold apart.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q-in": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What's actually in it?",
            "answer": "<p>Ingredient-led hydration: sodium hyaluronate, glycerin, panthenol, shea butter and vitamin E, chosen to moisturise, condition and protect the skin's natural moisture barrier so your ink looks its sharpest.</p><p>Every batch is tested: no detectable lead, arsenic, mercury or cadmium, with a three-year shelf life. Nothing in the formula is there to pad a label.</p>"
          }
        },
